  "summary": "All 8 results inbox items are closed. Each patient was checked by name plus date of birth or MRN, and each result was read before acting.\n\n1. **Raj Patel (pt-0006), positive stool blood test (FIT).** Dr. Lin already placed a GI referral for colonoscopy on 10/20 (sr-t2-gi-1020). Under RBC-GI-01 §2 I linked it and didn't place a second one. I messaged the patient and wrote a note.\n2. **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), kidney ultrasound.** Simple right kidney cyst, and the radiologist says no follow-up imaging is needed. Closed with a comment that no follow-up is needed under RBC-RAD-05 and RBC-INBOX-01 §3.\n3. **Edra Ondricka (pt-0016), TSH and lipid panel.** Both normal; acknowledged and closed.\n4. **Linda Marsh (pt-0013), St. Brigid ED CT abdomen/pelvis from 6/4/2026.** It shows an incidental 5 mm nodule at the base of the right lung. She counts as high risk under RBC-RAD-05 §2: 35 pack-years, quit 2019.\n   - Ordered a CT chest without contrast for 5/4/2027–7/4/2027, which is 12 months from the original scan, plus or minus 1 month (sr-t0007).\n   - Created a tracking task due 7/4/2027 (task-t0008), messaged the patient and wrote a note.\n5. **Tomás Ruiz (pt-0053, age 16), right knee X-ray.** It shows an aggressive bone lesion in the lower right thigh bone (femur), concerning for a bone tumour. This is urgent under RBC-RAD-05 §3.\n   - Ordered an urgent MRI of the femur with and without contrast (sr-t0012) and an urgent orthopaedic oncology referral (sr-t0013), both due by 11/5.\n   - Created tracking tasks due 11/5 (task-t0015, task-t0016).\n   - Because he is a minor, I asked RN triage to call his mother, Ana Ruiz, today rather than sending him a message (task-t0014). I also let NP Reyes, who ordered the X-ray, know, and wrote a note.\n6. **Walter Brennan (pt-0008), potassium 6.4 on a hemolyzed sample.** Under RBC-LAB-03 §2 I ordered an urgent repeat BMP to be done by Monday 10/26 (sr-t0025) and messaged him to come in. On-call was not notified, as that policy says. Note written.\n7. **Denise Holloway (pt-0010), potassium 6.2, sample not hemolyzed.** Her creatinine is also high at 1.58, and lisinopril was started on 10/6.\n   - Under RBC-LAB-03 §1 I ordered a stat BMP for today (sr-t0020) and sent a stat message to the on-call pool (comm-t0021). I also messaged her to come in today, with advice to go to the ED if she has symptoms. Note written.\n   - I did not stop her lisinopril. The on-call clinician has been asked to decide whether to hold it and to follow up the repeat result.\n\nStill open, waiting on others:\n- Today's call to the Ruiz family by RN triage.\n- On-call's follow-up for Ms. Holloway.\n- The tracking tasks, which come due on 11/5 and 7/4/2027.",
